WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.160
As far as action-packed shows from the 1990s go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.800
"Xena: Warrior Princess" is one of the&nbsp;
best. Xena, played by Lucy Lawless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.080
was given her own spin-off after a brief recurring&nbsp;
role in "Hercules: The Legendary Journeys."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.120
Creator Robert Tapert recognized how popular she&nbsp;
was with audiences, and "Xena: Warrior Princess"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.560
quickly became a cult favorite, running&nbsp;
for six seasons from 1995 to 2001.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.920
The swords-and-sandals epic doesn't just have the&nbsp;
hero facing off against evil warlords or Ares,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.760
the God of War, however. Xena often&nbsp;
battles demons and monsters too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.840
and considering the show was produced in&nbsp;
the 1990s, some of the practical effects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.800
look pretty great. It seems pretty clear that&nbsp;
"Xena" is ripe for a reboot, especially in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:49.200
time where "Wonder Woman" made $800 million at&nbsp;
the box office when it debuted back in 2017.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.240
So, why hasn't a "Xena" reboot happened yet?

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.720
Unsurprisingly, "Xena" fans have always been&nbsp;
vocal about their love for the hero, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.080
since many saw the clear subtext in the show that&nbsp;
she had a romance with Gabrielle, played by Renee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.840
O'Connor. In fact, their relationship was going to&nbsp;
be the main focus of a new "Xena" reboot in 2015&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:14.960
from "Lost" alumni Javier Grillo-Marxuach for NBC.&nbsp;
Grillo-Marxuach wrote on his Tumblr page in 2016,

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.920
"There is no reason to bring back 'Xena' if it&nbsp;
is not there for the purpose of fully exploring a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.440
relationship that could only be shown subtextually&nbsp;
in first-run syndication in the 1990s."

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.840
He also noted that the reboot would had some&nbsp;
kind of social relevance in its story, saying,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.360
"It will also express my view&nbsp;
of the world — which is only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.000
further informed by what is happening right now."

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.560
Unfortunately, in 2017, Grillo-Marxuach&nbsp;
parted ways with the "Xena" reboot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:46.160
due to creative differences with NBC. However,&nbsp;
Grillo-Marxuach told The Mary Sue that he remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.920
hopeful "Xena" will return to the screen&nbsp;
at some point in the future, explaining,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.920
"I truly hope that the alchemy of creative&nbsp;
elements that has to come together to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.560
possible either a reboot or revival of this&nbsp;
amazing property will someday coalesce."

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.280
When the news broke that the "Xena" reboot&nbsp;
wasn't going forward at NBC, the network's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.360
former Entertainment President Jennifer&nbsp;
Salke explained to The Hollywood Reporter,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.400
"Nothing is happening on that right&nbsp;
now. We looked at some material;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.600
we decided at that point that&nbsp;
it didn't warrant the reboot."

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.720
However, it wasn't all negative, as Salke pointed&nbsp;
out that "Xena" is a "beloved" property that might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.760
be rebooted some day. It all depends on who's&nbsp;
at the helm of the reboot, as Salke explained,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.720
"I'd never say never on that one because it's such&nbsp;
a beloved title, but the current incarnation of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.120
is dead [...] I need someone to come in with&nbsp;
a point of view about what they want to do."

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.800
In 2018, the pilot script for the reboot leaked&nbsp;
online to the Xena Movie Campaign Facebook page,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.360
but fans in the comments were disappointed&nbsp;
about what the script contained. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.640
one user lamented that Hercules had been changed&nbsp;
into a "heartless mercenary" in the script. Others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.120
felt that it had potential, especially where&nbsp;
Xena and Gabrielle's relationship was concerned.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.840
Fans also pointed out that a new "Xena" project&nbsp;
without Lucy Lawless wouldn't feel right.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.840
As for whether the star would ever come&nbsp;
back to the role, the answer is yes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.520
And we all have "Terminator: Dark&nbsp;
Fate" to thank. Lawless told Yahoo!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.000
Entertainment in July 2019 that seeing&nbsp;
Linda Hamilton return as Sarah Connor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.920
made her wonder why she couldn't do&nbsp;
the same with Xena. She revealed,

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.400
"I saw Linda being amazing, and I'm like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.960
'Why can't we do that?' Bring back me&nbsp;
and Renee [O'Connor] and reboot Xena!'"

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.360
While Lawless did admit that filming all the&nbsp;
action wasn't her favorite part of making "Xena:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.320
Warrior Princess," she said she'd happily&nbsp;
do it for a big-screen project, explaining,

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.720
"I always hated the action, and I don't&nbsp;
want to live that life. But for a movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.000
I can do a little bit."

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.960
Lawless even suggested that&nbsp;
a cinematic outing for Xena&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.920
could easily set up a brand-new hero, explaining,

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.480
"[If] it's about handing over the baton to Junior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:52.800
Xena or whatever — if you need mine and&nbsp;
Renee's help to do that, let's talk."

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.000
Lucy Lawless is in, and so are the fans. NBC&nbsp;
just needs to find a writer with a new vision.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.240
"Sounds simple enough."

